# Model

This folder contains the EMBER2024 malware classification and clustering pipeline.

## Setup

```bash
git clone https://github.com/FutureComputing4AI/EMBER2024.git
cd EMBER2024 && pip install .
cd ..
pip install lightgbm scikit-learn hdbscan umap-learn tqdm huggingface_hub
```

## Run

**Test run (PDF subset, ~200 MB):**

```bash
python model/ember2024_pipeline.py --data-dir ./ember_data --file-type PDF
```

**Limit training data to 1 GB:**

```bash
python model/ember2024_pipeline.py --data-dir ./ember_data --file-type PDF --max-gb 1
```

**Skip download if data is already on disk:**

```bash
python model/ember2024_pipeline.py --data-dir ./ember_data --skip-download --max-gb 1
```

**Full dataset:**

```bash
python model/ember2024_pipeline.py --data-dir ./ember_data --file-type all --max-gb 1
```

## Output Files

| File                           | Description                              |
| ------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------- |
| `lgbm_classifier.model`        | LightGBM malicious/benign classifier     |
| `random_forest_classifier.pkl` | Random Forest classifier                 |
| `kmeans_clusterer.pkl`         | K-Means clustering model                 |
| `hdbscan_clusterer.pkl`        | HDBSCAN clustering model                 |
| `cluster_scaler.pkl`           | Scaler used for clustering preprocessing |
| `cluster_pca.pkl`              | PCA used for clustering preprocessing    |
| `training_report.txt`          | Metrics summary from last training run   |

## Available File Types

| Type  | Size    | Notes                      |
| ----- | ------- | -------------------------- |
| PDF   | ~200 MB | Smallest, good for testing |
| ELF   | ~100 MB | Even smaller               |
| APK   | ~1.2 GB | Android apps               |
| Win32 | ~28 GB  | Windows 32-bit executables |
| Win64 | ~15 GB  | Windows 64-bit executables |
| all   | ~50+ GB | Full dataset               |
